OL,3,GNEWSAMillions signed off to cover SEND
OL,4,Adeficit
OL,5,
OL,6,FGloucestershire is set to receive more
OL,7,Fthan #100m from the government to cover
OL,8,F90% of its Special Educational Needs
OL,9,Fand Disabilities (SEND) deficit.
OL,11,FGloucestershire County Council leader,
OL,12,FLisa Spivey, said the #112.2m of
OL,13,Ffunding was an "important moment" for
OL,14,Fthe county, and will enable children to
OL,15,Fget "the right support, at the right
OL,16,Ftime, in the right place".
OL,18,FThe council will still have to find an
OL,19,Fadditional #12.5m this financial year
OL,20,Fto balance the SEND budget.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
